  %% Regression mechanism, confirmed by source + git blame (not an assumption):
  %% - IS_ACTIVE_FOR_REPO(url) = get_repo_use_cache(url), a PER-USER/PER-REPO row in
  %%   ORTEC user persistence (ZCL_ABAPGIT_PERSISTENCE_ORTEC). READ TABLE against an
  %%   internal table keyed by url; missing row -> initial structure -> use_cache = false.
  %%   Any read exception is also silently mapped to false (CATCH cx_root).
  %% - Default is OFF for every repo/user that has not explicitly opened Repository
  %%   Settings and toggled "Use Persistent Object Cache"
  %%   (zcl_abapgit_gui_page_sett_repo.clas.abap calling set_use_repo_cache).
  %% - Result: the sparse/cached filtered walk (branch labelled "fast" above) is only
  %%   reached for repos where a user has explicitly opted in. Everyone else silently
  %%   gets the exact same "full get_files_remote()" cost as before any Ortec
  %%   optimization existed -- with no error, warning, or visible indicator.
  %% - This switch pre-existed (since 3e964850 / 81345469) ONLY for the WRITE-side
  %%   ZCL_ABAPGIT_ORTEC_FASTPATH pull/persist logic, where opt-in is a reasonable
  %%   safety gate for mutating ZAOG_* tables. e61fcb11 additionally attached the
  %%   READ-ONLY, non-mutating filter-walk optimization to that SAME switch, so
  %%   disabling (or never enabling) the write-side cache also silently disables the
  %%   always-safe read-side rendering speed-up.
